Alright what these commands do something like LS? 
It's going to list down all of the files present in current working directory. 
Exa. 
$ ls -l 
It's going to list down files with detailed information like size, date and all. 
there will be more options with '-' here. Such as, ls -t, ls -ltr, ls -ld, ls -lt, ls -1.... these are basic I can try. 

Then comes CD-
CD is going to change directory, this can change directory. 
cd /etc 
It's going to change current directory to 'etc'

GREP 
This command specifically searched for pattern in file. 
if you type GREP - .........
infront of '-' this command will paste the pattern which you have mentioned there infront of '-' symbol. 
exa. 
grep - e,, it's going to put result on new line. 
Usually grep was attached to the first commands output. 
Exa. 
ls -ltr | grep 'python'
It suppose to show files and all details regarding python patter. 

